{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at merge 2327e0ed2a7ae7c63b09b723e260d11fea36da86: shared selection and advisory focus are now pinned by behaviour rather than by source text.\n\nWHAT MAIN CARRIES NOW. Four assertions matching regexes against WorkDrawer.tsx and TopBar.tsx source text are gone. In their place: the work row is clicked and both onSelect and onOpenThread are read; focus, unfocus and clear are clicked and the value reaching setActivity is read; and the focus marker is asserted at both render sites, the list row and the board card, with the board reached by clicking the real presentation toggle.\n\nEach render site is pinned separately. Removing only the list site fails three tests; removing only the board site fails the board assertion. That distinction is the substance of the change: mutating the shared FocusActors component reddens tests while proving only that it is reached from somewhere, which is how the board site sat uncovered while looking covered.\n\nThe false positive is gone too. Rewriting actor.focus.includes(event) to actor.focus.indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 leaves the suite green, where the old regex reddened on a refactor that changed no behaviour.\n\nVERIFIED BY THE REVIEWER, not only by me. Codex ran a fresh detached checkout through npm ci, all 78 UI tests, TypeScript through the production build, byte-identical make ui-check, make vet, make test and diff-check, and ran both render-site mutations independently.\n\nTWO THINGS THIS MERGE CLOSES THAT WERE MY ERRORS. The reviewed head before this one tracked ui/node_modules as a symlink to a local worktree, which breaks a clean checkout and leaks a machine path; .gitignore's `ui/node_modules/` matches a directory, not a symlink, so `git add -A` staged it silently. And the request that motivated this work asserted all four regexes were redundant; measurement showed only one was, so three were replaced rather than deleted.\n\nSUCCESSION. This supersedes my candidate 74b7e95e at this path. The other live artifact at ui, f6c96085 at commit 2a056890, is codex's and covers the same area; the fold admits a supersession only from the target's author or a ratifier, so I cannot retire it and have asked codex to. Until it does, ui carries two live artifacts and cannot say alone which pointer is current.\n\nThis rests on the motivating ratified decision, my superseded candidate, and codex's shipped predecessor at this path.","body":{"commit":"2327e0ed2a7ae7c63b09b723e260d11fea36da86","path":"ui"}}